{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired and deployed the UDP collector on node1. It now validates nonnegative decimal fields, durably appends valid readings, persists duplicate detection across process/node restarts, records malformed datagrams separately, and starts automatically on boot. Both nodes were rebooted sequentially and fully recovered. Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Preserved the original collector as collector.py.pre-repair.","Implemented Python 2.5-compatible validation, durable writes, persistent duplicate detection, and malformed.csv logging.","Installed and enabled the udp-meter-collector SysV service.","Tested valid, duplicate, malformed, and negative-value datagrams from node2.","Verified the original west,1,42 reading remained intact.","Restarted the collector and verified duplicate state persisted.","Rebooted node1 and node2 individually, verifying changed boot identities and recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Valid datagrams append, duplicate meter/sequence pairs are ignored, and malformed datagrams are isolated without stopping collection.","command_ids":["cmd-14ada532884148d5","cmd-3a4fd1e296d2411a","cmd-68e6c293fa2244ac"],"summary":"Five test datagrams were sent from node2. Final assertions show valid_append=PASS, duplicates=PASS, malformed_separate=PASS, with malformed payloads decoded separately."},{"requirement":"Previously recorded data is preserved across collector restarts.","command_ids":["cmd-8ed39956a8044b51","cmd-05c1c118be264f02","cmd-c89759a99f1746ab","cmd-38968d3c11b347b4"],"summary":"The original west,1,42 record was observed before repair. After a collector PID change, existing keys remained deduplicated while a new key appended successfully."},{"requirement":"Collector runs persistently on UDP port 9098 using legacy-compatible software.","command_ids":["cmd-60a7c3fd37a14b29","cmd-68e6c293fa2244ac"],"summary":"Shows the Python 2.5-compatible collector running, listening on UDP 9098, enabled at boot, and passing all final assertions."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart: healthy baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data.","command_ids":["cmd-8cc7e36a2e2f4610","cmd-86893fbae6da4970","cmd-a0ba0785ed154c4b","cmd-5b8e4447778e47ad"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 45455a77-0c9d-48f2-91d0-9926b25735e2 to 1b5e4c63-1751-458a-a5a1-be172b037ba5. The service, listener, exact CSV hash, readings, and malformed records recovered."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart: healthy baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered sending capability/data.","command_ids":["cmd-6a46f8b3cc544d68","cmd-46ed4cdfb21a470e","cmd-da71778913ad4427","cmd-5515328d73b84e74","cmd-102fa2f1be0b4e84","cmd-68e6c293fa2244ac"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 76e8c8cb-63be-420e-b049-801ab2e185db to cb71f7af-0336-4c50-a41a-88c99755627d. Networking and sample data recovered, and post-reboot UDP traffic was received with duplicate suppression intact."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel remain unchanged.","command_ids":["cmd-e291da1496c54518","cmd-702ee8aa383d4d78","cmd-68e6c293fa2244ac","cmd-21fe7ee1d7be4f13"],"summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 7.10 with kernel 2.6.22-14-generic before and after the work."}]}
